# Build context for packaging/docker/Dockerfile: the workspace manifests, the crate sources that
# `cargo build -p cadcraft-cli` links, the contributor tables crates/ui-egui bakes in at build time,
# the built web site the image serves (dist/web), and packaging/docker/nginx/default.conf.
# Everything else stays out of the upload.
.git
.github
target
target-*
plan
plans
log
temp
.claude
# Keep dist/web — the site the image serves — and drop the release artifacts beside it. Trunk's
# staging directory is only there while a build is running and must never end up in the image.
dist/release
dist/web/.stage
# Not needed by the image; apps/cadcraft (the desktop app) is not built here.
# The CI workflow checks craft-fonts out here for the web build, which runs before this build.
craft-fonts
docs
examples
assets
ROADMAP.md
